## Installation

```bash
pip install {{ package_name }}
```

## Usage

Once installed, the tasks from this package will be automatically available in invoke-toolkit:

```bash
intk -l
```

You should see a collection named `{{ collection_name }}` with the available tasks.

### Available Tasks

- `hello` - Say hello to someone

Example:

```bash
intk {{ collection_name }}.hello --name "Alice"
```

## Running Standalone

You can also run this package standalone without installing it system-wide, using `uvx`:

```bash
cd path/to/{{ package_slug }}
uvx --from . invoke-toolkit -l
```

This allows you to test and use the package's tasks in an isolated environment without affecting your system Python installation.

## Development

To set up the development environment:

```bash
git clone <repository-url>
cd {{ package_name }}
uv venv
uv pip install -e .
```

